# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Force LF in the WORKING TREE, not just in the repository.
#
# `* text=auto` on its own normalizes to LF on commit but checks out the
# platform's native endings, so on Windows with core.autocrlf=true the working
# tree gets CRLF. The repo stays clean and the problem is invisible in a diff,
# but anything packaged from that checkout ships CRLF.
#
# That is not cosmetic for this repo. charts/codesys-app renders a container
# `command` that is executed by /bin/sh. A carriage return on an executable
# line makes the shell read `set -e\r` and `CFG=...cfg\r`, so the config path
# picks up a trailing CR, the guarded greps miss, the runtime starts without
# its boot application registered, and the tester serves nothing while logging
# almost nothing. Measured 2026-09-26: a chart tarred from a Windows checkout
# carried CRLF on 248 lines of templates/deployment.yaml.
#
# eol=lf makes the checkout LF everywhere, so packaging is safe from any host.
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.tpl   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
